# SfxLab bench v1: layer id name type dur seed key=value... (dur 0 = endless) · range id param lo hi [note] · bind signal id|* param [lo hi] [rel] [steps=N | scale=<chord>]
# pyretic v3 — the searching mix, voiced by register and by chord tone, arm-agnostic. One bass bed at C2 and nothing else
# below C3. Four voices at C3-C4, one per chord tone of the harmonic series (root, third, fifth, seventh), each brought in by
# its tone.* signal: however the motions are spread over the arms, a ratio near 2/4/8 sings the root, near 3/6 the fifth,
# near 5 the third, near 7 the seventh, and a ratio gliding between integers walks through them. The cloud is the chord that
# forms: it grows with the number of motions (stack), stays a soft cluster while the ratios are detuned and gathers once every
# engaged ratio is an integer (coherence). The orb colours everything: its swing opens the voices' low-pass, its curl makes
# the fifth shimmer and the third phase, its speed phases the root. fit (the reach hint) steadies the notes: a wrong reach
# leaves the root and third wobbling, the right one lets them ring clean.
bench 1
root 65.4064
layer bed pyretic/pyretic_synth_00001_loop 7 0.0000 1001 level=0.35000 attack=0.30000 release=0.60000 pitch=-5.17941 cutoff=1.00000 echo=0.00000 reverb=0.00000 drive=0.00000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=1.00000 keyed=1 file=pyretic/pyretic_synth_00001_loop.ogg
layer third pyretic/pyretic_synth_00008_loop 7 0.0000 1002 level=0.00000 attack=0.25000 release=0.50000 pitch=-8.55300 cutoff=1.00000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=0.40000 keyed=1 file=pyretic/pyretic_synth_00008_loop.ogg
layer root pyretic/pyretic_synth_00012 7 0.0000 1003 level=0.00000 attack=0.30000 release=0.60000 pitch=19.03000 cutoff=0.80000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=0.20000 keyed=1 file=pyretic/pyretic_synth_00012.ogg
layer fifth tones 1 0.0000 1004 level=0.00000 attack=0.30000 release=0.60000 pitch=22.02000 cutoff=0.70000 reverb=0.35000 timbre=2.00000 bank=0.40000 tilt=-0.30000 keyed=1
layer seventh tones 1 0.0000 1009 level=0.00000 attack=0.35000 release=0.70000 pitch=24.68800 cutoff=0.60000 reverb=0.40000 timbre=1.00000 bank=0.50000 tilt=-0.50000 keyed=1
layer cloud cloud 0 0.0000 1005 level=0.00000 attack=0.80000 release=1.20000 pitch=3.00000 cutoff=0.70000 reverb=0.40000 voices=5.00000 gather=0.50000 drift=0.20000 timbre=0.50000 chord=2.00000 sub=0.00000 keyed=1
layer fire pyretic/fire_loop 5 0.0000 1006 level=0.00000 attack=0.30000 release=0.60000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=0.50000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=pyretic/fire_loop.ogg
layer sparks pyretic/match_sparks_ignition_00001 5 2.9445 1007 level=0.25000 attack=0.00200 release=0.02000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=1.00000 keyed=2 on=lock file=pyretic/match_sparks_ignition_00001.ogg
layer woosh pyretic/heat_woosh_major_chord_00001 5 6.1288 1008 level=0.18000 attack=0.05000 release=0.06000 pitch=-0.26000 cutoff=0.70000 keyed=2 on=accept file=pyretic/heat_woosh_major_chord_00001.ogg
range bed level 0.08 0.35 rests at 0.35, steps back to 0.2 once the arms move and a further 0.12 as the machine fills (stack); no echo or reverb on the bass
range third level 0 0.4 the third: synth8 down to E4
range root level 0 0.22 the root: synth12 up two octaves to C4 (at C3 its partials still carried sub-bass)
range fifth level 0 0.15 the fifth: an additive tone at G4, brighter with tension
range seventh level 0 0.12 the seventh: a darker tone at Bb4
range fifth bank 0.2 0.8 harmonic richness
range cloud level 0 0.3 the chord, growing with the number of motions; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud gather 0.5 1 a soft cluster while searching, the chord once every ratio is an integer
range fire level 0 0.5 the near-miss flicker: rises with the pinned spell's score
bind stir bed level 0.35 0.2
bind stack bed level 0 -0.12 rel
bind orb.accel bed drive 0 0.03
bind tone.root root level 0 0.22
bind tone.third third level 0 0.4
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.15
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.12
bind tension fifth bank 0.2 0.8
bind stack cloud level 0 0.3
bind coherence cloud gather 0.5 1
bind radiance cloud reverb 0.3 0.7
bind fit root shimmer 0.3 0
bind fit third shimmer 0.3 0
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.3 0.9
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.3 1
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.35 0.9
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.3 0.8
bind orb.curl fifth bank_shimmer 0 0.6
bind orb.curl third phaser 0 0.7
bind orb.speed root phaser 0 0.6
bind score fire level 0 0.5
note v3 register plan. Below C3 there is only the bed (synth1 at C2). The notes are chord tones, not arms: root = synth12 at
note C4, third = synth8 at E4, fifth = a sine-plus-bank tone at G4, seventh = a darker tone at Bb4. Each is brought in by its
note tone.* signal (the reach sitting on that pitch class, from any arm), so the mix is arm-agnostic like the tuning itself.
note cloud: level with stack (one motion = a whisper, six = the chord), gather with coherence (detuned = soft cluster,
note integers = chord), reverb with radiance (Z). The orb's radius opens every voice's low-pass (wide swing = bright, tight
note = dark), its curl shimmers the fifth and phases the third, its speed phases the root. fit steadies the root and third.
note fire: the pinned spell's score is its level (the near-miss flicker). Textures per spell live in the spell files, low-passed.
note Spells do not set the voices; they set the bed, the cloud's chord, their textures and one-shots.
